ite","checks":"write","code_quality":"write","contents":"write","copilot_requests":"write","deployments":"write","discussions":"write","drives":"write","issues":"write","merge_queues":"write","metadata":"read","models":"read","packages":"write","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6083713414","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/pull/56#issuecomment-6083713414","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/56","id":6083713414,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSN6Nm88AAAABap4Zhg","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-09T15:13:15Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T15:13:15Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** C\n**Automated operational score:** 70/100 — CRITICAL — APPROVE_WITH_COMMENTS\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **CRITICAL · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · NSG permits unrestricted inbound SSH (TCP/22) from the public internet**\n  - Category rationale: The NSG security rule 'AllowSSH' explicitly permits inbound TCP/22 from source 0.0.0.0/0 at priority 300, which is evaluated before the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096. This creates a direct, unrestricted path from the public internet to SSH on any resource attached to this NSG. The code comment 'TC02: Deliberately unrestricted SSH access' documents awareness but does not constitute a justification or compensating control under SEC-001. The tfsec scanner findings AVD-AZU-0047 and AVD-AZU-0050 independently confirm ingress from the public internet and SSH exposure.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_network_security_group.nsg, security_rule 'AllowSSH': priority = 300, direction = \"Inbound\", access = \"Allow\", protocol = \"Tcp\", source_address_prefix = \"0.0.0.0/0\", destination_port_range = \"22\". DenyAllInbound is at priority 4096 and is therefore evaluated after the Allow rule. tfsec findings AVD-AZU-0047 and AVD-AZU-0050 on the same resource corroborate.\n  - Analysis: The security rule 'AllowSSH' in azurerm_network_security_group.nsg is configured with source_address_prefix = \"0.0.0.0/0\", destination_port_range = \"22\", access = \"Allow\", and priority = 300 (Inbound). Because NSG rules are evaluated in ascending priority order, this Allow rule takes effect before the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096. Any resource associated with this NSG — now or in the future — will accept SSH connections from any IP address on the internet. The inline comment acknowledges this is deliberate ('TC02: Deliberately unrestricted SSH access') but the PR and supplied documentation do not establish a business justification or compensating control that satisfies SEC-001.\n  - Impact: Any host attached to nsg-demo-ai is reachable over SSH from any public IP address. Even without an active VM today, applying this NSG configuration makes SSH exploitation trivially accessible the moment any resource is attached. This violates the principle of least-privilege network access and policy SEC-001 (no public exposure without explicit justification).\n  - Recommendation: Restrict source_address_prefix to a known operator IP range or managed jump-host CIDR (e.g., a corporate egress prefix or Azure Bastion subnet). If SSH access is required for research purposes, document the specific source range and add a PR-level justification. If interactive SSH is not required for TC01 (network-only case), remove the AllowSSH rule entirely and rely on the DenyAllInbound baseline.\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **SEC-001** — No resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified. (finding F-001)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6083713414/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravat